_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104425","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104425.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104425.patch","merged_at":"2025-03-24T15:05:20Z"},"body":"Move the individual message handlers to separate functions, to make it easier to follow the `_parse_message` function. The function is also more efficient as it only performs a single hash lookup for the handler and then dispatches to the member function rather than multiple string compares.\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n>\r\n> If you select the **hide whitespace** option, the PR is much simpler to review as the code and behaviour is identical, with the introduction of a hash table to store handlers for each of the messages and to dispatch them in the `_parse_message` function.\r\n\r\n## Background\r\n\r\nThis wasn't a random refactor, as I was evaluating macOS embedded game window support, and that naturally led me through the debugger code and handlers, as we will need to serialise events from the host Godot editor to the spawned game. ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","r